inant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\,(1\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,2\\,(3\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 4)\\,+\\,5\\,(3\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =0(-2)\\,-\\,2\\,(-6)\\,+\\,5\\,(-7) \\\\  & =0+12-35 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cd6328a-133b-5e12-8514-1efaa6b6d672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cd6328a-133b-5e12-8514-1efaa6b6d672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298022} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ebcaea2-b965-5e9e-8bcc-7aeba6a2af03" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299010}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e752a1da-5c2f-551a-a669-66eee02c7b08" :question/math-academy-id "q-317317" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,0,-2⟩$ and $c=⟨5,6,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\